<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TestCaseEntity>
   <description>Mirrors Jira PT-269 (manually tested/passed 6/17/2026 by Lejla): when show-react-portal-poc is OFF, the React shell must not render, and users must still be able to reach SCiEnable and SCiSupplier via their existing direct URLs without disruption. PT-269 itself notes the exact fallback behavior (redirect/404/&quot;coming soon&quot;) was still an open PM question as of the source ticket — this script only asserts the shell does NOT render and that direct-URL access still works, not a specific fallback UI. Uses ffOffSupplierEmail (Regression profile), an account confirmed flagged-out as of PT-266 (6/17/2026) — reconfirm current flag state with Lejla/PostHog before trusting a failure as a real regression vs. a stale flag assumption. Updated 10/1/2026 now that the 2FA blocker is resolved: this flag-off account (supplier.scienable) lands on SCiSupplier's Switch Company page served directly (/scf/accountSwitcher.htm) — no shell, no iframe, so the script uses top-level locators only. Loops through all 32 of this account's companies via `Data Files/FlagOffSupplierCompanies` (a different list from the flag-on account), confirming shell chrome stays absent for each one. Returns to the switcher by navigating to its URL (captured right after login) rather than a header link, because some companies land on a &quot;complete your user profile&quot; page with no header menu — do not click Save there, it changes the shared account. Never point ffOffSupplierEmail at a flag-ON account (e.g. gpm.scienable) — the shell-not-present check would fail for the wrong reason. First full pass 10/1/2026. Step 2 (direct SCiEnable URL check) is unaffected and unchanged.</description>
   <name>TC_FeatureFlag_ShellNotRendered_FallbackWorks</name>
   <tag></tag>
   <comment></comment>
   <recordOption>OTHER</recordOption>
   <testCaseGuid>b3c4d5e6-f7a8-4b3c-9d4e-5f6a7b8c9d0e</testCaseGuid>
</TestCaseEntity>
